/E (For polymorphism, the more interesting part is runtime polymorphism. I stored a Mage object and a Warrior object inside a Character[] array and called displayInfo\(\)/calculateRegenRate\(\) on the array. Even though the declared type of the array is Character, at runtime it still picks the correct overridden version depending on what object is actually in the array.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [9]
>>
